        ['The cost C cedis of hiring a canopy is partly constant and partly varies as the number of hours h. It costs GH₵ 45 for 5 hours and GH₵ 54 for 8 hours. (a) Find the relationship between C and h. (b) Find the cost for 14 hours.', ['C = a + bh', 'b = 3', 'a = 30', 'Cost GH₵ 72'], '(a) C = a + bh. 45 = a + 5b and 54 = a + 8b. Subtracting: 9 = 3b, so b = 3 and a = 30. C = 30 + 3h. (b) C = 30 + 3 × 14 = GH₵ 72.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['The cost C cedis of hiring a canopy is partly constant and partly varies as the number of hours h. It costs GH₵ 58 for 4 hours and GH₵ 66 for 8 hours. (a) Find the relationship between C and h. (b) Find the cost for 19 hours.', ['C = a + bh', 'b = 2', 'a = 50', 'Cost GH₵ 88'], '(a) C = a + bh. 58 = a + 4b and 66 = a + 8b. Subtracting: 8 = 4b, so b = 2 and a = 50. C = 50 + 2h. (b) C = 50 + 2 × 19 = GH₵ 88.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['The cost C cedis of hiring a canopy is partly constant and partly varies as the number of hours h. It costs GH₵ 20 for 5 hours and GH₵ 26 for 8 hours. (a) Find the relationship between C and h. (b) Find the cost for 18 hours.', ['C = a + bh', 'b = 2', 'a = 10', 'Cost GH₵ 46'], '(a) C = a + bh. 20 = a + 5b and 26 = a + 8b. Subtracting: 6 = 3b, so b = 2 and a = 10. C = 10 + 2h. (b) C = 10 + 2 × 18 = GH₵ 46.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['The cost C cedis of hiring a canopy is partly constant and partly varies as the number of hours h. It costs GH₵ 35 for 5 hours and GH₵ 38 for 6 hours. (a) Find the relationship between C and h. (b) Find the cost for 15 hours.', ['C = a + bh', 'b = 3', 'a = 20', 'Cost GH₵ 65'], '(a) C = a + bh. 35 = a + 5b and 38 = a + 6b. Subtracting: 3 = 1b, so b = 3 and a = 20. C = 20 + 3h. (b) C = 20 + 3 × 15 = GH₵ 65.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
    ],
    'SHS 2: Arithmetic and geometric progressions' => [
        ['In an arithmetic progression (AP), consecutive terms have', ['a common difference', 'a common ratio', 'the same value always', 'squares as terms'], 'A', 'Remember: d.', 1],
        ['In a geometric progression (GP), consecutive terms have', ['a common difference', 'a common ratio', 'random values', 'equal sums'], 'B', 'Remember: r.', 1],
        ['The nth term of an AP is', ['arⁿ⁻¹', 'a + nd', 'a + (n − 1)d', 'n(a + l)/2'], 'C', 'General term.', 2],
        ['The nth term of a GP is', ['a + (n − 1)d', 'arⁿ', 'a/r', 'arⁿ⁻¹'], 'D', 'General term.', 2],
