        ['A garden is in the shape of a sector of a circle of radius 21 m and angle 60°. A path is laid along the curved edge only. Taking π = 22/7, find (a) the area of the garden, (b) the length of the curved edge, (c) the perimeter of the garden. (d) A circular pond of radius 7 m is dug in it. Find the remaining area.', ['Sector area', 'Arc length', 'Perimeter', 'Pond area', 'Remaining area'], '(a) (60/360) × 22/7 × 21² = 231 m². (b) (60/360) × 2 × 22/7 × 21 = 22 m. (c) 22 + 2 × 21 = 64 m. (d) Pond = 22/7 × 7² = 154 m²; remaining = 77 m².', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A garden is in the shape of a sector of a circle of radius 14 m and angle 60°. A path is laid along the curved edge only. Taking π = 22/7, find (a) the area of the garden, (b) the length of the curved edge, (c) the perimeter of the garden. (d) A circular pond of radius 7 m is dug in it. Find the remaining area.', ['Sector area', 'Arc length', 'Perimeter', 'Pond area', 'Remaining area'], '(a) (60/360) × 22/7 × 14² = 102.67 m². (b) (60/360) × 2 × 22/7 × 14 = 14.67 m. (c) 14.67 + 2 × 14 = 42.67 m. (d) Pond = 22/7 × 7² = 154 m²; remaining = −51.33 m².', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
