        ['The marks of some candidates are grouped as (class: frequency) 1–10: 14, 11–20: 4, 21–30: 12, 31–40: 4, 41–50: 6, 51–60: 4. (a) Construct a cumulative frequency table. (b) Calculate the mean mark, correct to 1 decimal place. (c) Describe how you would estimate the median from an ogive.', ['Cumulative frequencies', 'Class marks', 'Mean 24.6', 'Ogive method'], '(a) Cumulative frequencies: 14, 18, 30, 34, 40, 44 (total 44). (b) Class marks 5.5, 15.5, …, 55.5; mean = Σfx ÷ Σf = 24.6. (c) Plot cumulative frequency against upper class boundaries (10.5, 20.5, …), draw a smooth S-curve, find 22 (half of 44) on the vertical axis and read across to the curve and down to the marks axis.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['The marks of some candidates are grouped as (class: frequency) 1–10: 5, 11–20: 14, 21–30: 12, 31–40: 9, 41–50: 15, 51–60: 11. (a) Construct a cumulative frequency table. (b) Calculate the mean mark, correct to 1 decimal place. (c) Describe how you would estimate the median from an ogive.', ['Cumulative frequencies', 'Class marks', 'Mean 32.8', 'Ogive method'], '(a) Cumulative frequencies: 5, 19, 31, 40, 55, 66 (total 66). (b) Class marks 5.5, 15.5, …, 55.5; mean = Σfx ÷ Σf = 32.8. (c) Plot cumulative frequency against upper class boundaries (10.5, 20.5, …), draw a smooth S-curve, find 33 (half of 66) on the vertical axis and read across to the curve and down to the marks axis.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['The marks of some candidates are grouped as (class: frequency) 1–10: 11, 11–20: 11, 21–30: 15, 31–40: 12, 41–50: 5, 51–60: 3. (a) Construct a cumulative frequency table. (b) Calculate the mean mark, correct to 1 decimal place. (c) Describe how you would estimate the median from an ogive.', ['Cumulative frequencies', 'Class marks', 'Mean 25.1', 'Ogive method'], '(a) Cumulative frequencies: 11, 22, 37, 49, 54, 57 (total 57). (b) Class marks 5.5, 15.5, …, 55.5; mean = Σfx ÷ Σf = 25.1. (c) Plot cumulative frequency against upper class boundaries (10.5, 20.5, …), draw a smooth S-curve, find 28.5 (half of 57) on the vertical axis and read across to the curve and down to the marks axis.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
